    "AND is the gate you want for a simple enable: data on one input, a control line on the other.",
    "Same pin arrangement as the 74HC00, 74HC32 and 74HC86. The only way to tell them apart on a board is the marking, so check before you assume the logic.",
    "Unused inputs must be tied high or low. A floating CMOS input oscillates and drags supply current.",
    "HC inputs need a level near their own rail. Driving a 5 V part from 3.3 V logic wants the HCT version."
